{
  "_comment": [
    "Data quality rule thresholds, per tag (\u00a7384). Retuning a limit is a row",
    "change here, not an edit to engine/quality.py (\u00a7341).",
    "",
    "Rate-of-change limits are set above what the PROCESS can do, so that what",
    "they catch is the instrument rather than the plant. Note they are sized for",
    "the simulator's demonstration timing, where a full cold start-up runs in",
    "150 s; a three-hour start-up moves far more slowly and these limits stay",
    "conservative. The reverse would not be true, so they are set for the fast",
    "case deliberately.",
    "",
    "The cross-tag pair the build plan suggests is feedwater flow against main",
    "steam flow. The simulator has no main steam flow tag, so the equivalent",
    "real relationship available here is feedwater flow against gross",
    "generation: steam flow tracks load, and at 210 MW the unit takes about",
    "670 t/h, giving roughly 3.19 t/h per MW. It is gated on load, because the",
    "relationship does not hold while the boiler is being filled with the",
    "breaker open."
  ],
  "rules": [
